### Inverse Method

The solutions {_y_} of the equations {_u_ = _F_(_y_)} form a sequence of independent random deviates with cumulative distribution function _F_(_y_). (If _F_(_y_) has a discontinuity at \(y\) = \(y\)0, then whenever \(u\) is such that _F_(_y_0 = 0)<_u_<_F_(_y_), select \(y\)0 as the corresponding deviate.) Generally the inverse method is not practical unless the inverse function \(y\) = _F_-1(_u_) can be obtained explicitly or can be conveniently approximated.

